15732:
 Aha. Well I can just add Fawn Dungeon to the unreleased list then, since it had no carts made back in the day.
I'm kind of torn on the BASICarts. On one hand, they did certainly get made, but it sounds like very, very few copies were back in the 80s. Granted the line between a homebrew title and a third party release is incredibly blurry on the Bally, so I mean... it wouldn't hurt to at least list when they were available on demand, if not necessarily running down the list of every single one made at the time.
1978 still eludes me though. Does anyone know what games the system launched with?
I'm also rather interested in other aspects of documenting the system's history - internal documents from Bally or Astrovision that may still exist (and could find their way to some kind of publicly available archive), interviews with the hardware engineers and software devs for the cart games like Jamie Fenton, etc. I've been working on that kind of stuff with the RCA Studio II and it's been a treasure trove, but I've also encountered dead-ends from people who have passed away - it would make sense to try and get as much stuff down and recorded as possible, while they're still around, and any remaining documents might still exist. Ballyalley.com is a real good source, but if there's any more info potentially out there it ought to be found!
