Astrocade game release dates


 









Hi
all, as part of an ongoing effort to document the history of
the early video game scene in the US, I've been trying
to track down release dates as accurately as possible for
classic consoles. In the case of the Astrocade, this has
manifested in using the handful of months provided mainly
out of the Computer Entertainer/Video Game Update industry
newsletter, and the ads and news from the Arcadian
newsletter scans (as well as a little bit of information
from the Weekly Television Digest industry periodicals
I've got access to). So far this is what I've got -
1978 is really messy, so any clarification there would be
lovely! Anything bold is something I'm pretty confident
in.
1978:
(9 releases)Last
2 weeks of Dec 77 into January - System started shipping
after orders started coming in fall of 77, launched w/
dealer
democart
and 3 others + 3 more later in Jan? (from tv digest
12-26-77)January:
Dealer
Democart (sold broadly in 83 via arcadian),May:
Baseball/Tennis, Elementary Math
(advertised as launch games in 9-19-77 tv digest, but
Arcadian notes on shelves in May issue)August:
Sea Wolf? (or earlier)Early
Fall?: 280 Zzzap, Panzer Attack,October:
Tiny
BASIC (Arcadian
2-1)Late
Fall?: Clowns/Brickyard, Blackjack/Poker
1979:
(6 releases) January:
 Amazing
Maze(Arcadian
1-03, though advertised as being available in the fall in
volume 00), Football
(Late
Dec to early Jan)February:
Star
Battle
(Arcadian 1-05)October:
Bally Pinball
(rereleased 1981 as Astrocade Pinball), Space
Invaders (later
Astro Battle w/ Astrocade) - 1-11 arcadian?:
Letter Match (by august via ad in 1-09 arcadian),

1980:
(1 release) - Bally announces sale of home division at Jan
CES to Fidelity Electronics (1-14-80 TV Digest) sale falls
through in March (arcadian); Astrovision agrees to buy
AugustOctober:
Dog
Patch(last
Bally labeled release),
1981:(7
releases, 2 of them homebrew)August:
Galaxian(Galactic
Invasion) - Arcadian 3-10September:
Biorhythm,
Grand Prix/Demolition Derby, Astrovision BASIC (Arcadian
3-12)October:
Space
Fortress
(arcadian 3-12, def out by Jan CES)November:
Blue
RAM Extended BASIC
(4-1 arcadian)December:
Machine
Language Manager
(Arcadian 4-2)
1982:
(5 brand new releases, 2 3rd
party/homebrew)March:
Galactic Invasion? (Galaxian in 1981, 4-4 arcadian indicates
was available by jan ces)May:
Blue
Ram 8K Extended BASIC
(Arcadian 4-7)August:
Incredible
WizardSeptember:
Pirate’s ChaseOctober:
Artillery
Duel,
?:
ICBM Attack (Mentioned arcadian 4-9, July
issue)
1983:
(8 releases, 6 3rd party/homebrew)March
6: Muncher
(5-5
Arcadian, orders opened Jan - technically unofficial
unreleased Pac-Man game)April:
Treasure
Cove(May in CE? But April in Arcadian 5-6)July:
Blast
Droids
(Arcadian 5-9)August:
Solar
Conqueror(Sept
83?), Cosmic
Raiders
(Arcadian 5-10)September:
Ms.
Candy Man(Arcadian
5-11)Sept.
24:
Sneaky SnakeDecember:
Sea
Devil (Ad
Arcadian 6-2)
1984:
(1 release, homebrew/3rd party)March:
Maze Man (ad in Arcadian 6-5)
1985:(9
releases, all homebrew releases of prototypes or third party
games)May:
Life
(Ad in Arcadian 7-1)December:
Soccer,
Bowling, Checkers, Conan, Music Maker (Arcadian
7-2), also available are Songs
(by Moses), Video Story Book, Missile Attack(ICBM modded for
standard controls)
Unreleased/prototype:
Drag Race, Chess, Creative Crayon























